# Pi keeps its per-project work state in .pi/: active and archived goals, the
# goal event log, ledger checkpoints and lock files. That is the state of one
# session on one machine, not repository material, so it stays out of the tree.
# .pi/settings.json is deliberately tracked: it declares this package (`..`) and
# the vendored ./pi-simple-world-model, without which a clone of this workspace
# has no world model checks and no `eyg` tool.
.pi/goals/
.pi/.goals-pool-snapshot.json

# pi installs project-local packages under .pi/npm/: an install artefact of this
# machine (the npm tree of the declarations in .pi/settings.json), not source.
.pi/npm/

# session state: task STATE files and scratch, never tracked
.ai-work/

# Scratch for a runner this machine names with EYG_CODEMODE_RUNNER. A build of the
# language CLI is around 105 MB, so a binary parked here stays untracked.
.local/

# A probe whose write is allowed lands here when it is run with its working directory in the
# tree; it is evidence of a run, never something to commit.
eyg-probe-refused.txt
